{"id":"mahabharata-13-024","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":24,"title":"चतुर्विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 24 · The rules of rites for gods and ancestors","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks for the rules laid down by the sages for the rites to the gods and the ancestors and for gifts. Bhishma gives them at length, saying that those who hold back the dues of the lowly and those who break up what is made ready for a good person go to hell, and tells of the duties of the giver and the receiver.","kn":"ಶ್ರಾದ್ಧ, ದೈವ, ಧರ್ಮ ಕಾರ್ಯಗಳ, ದಾನದ ಋಷಿ ವಿಹಿತ ನಿಯಮ ಹೇಳಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿನಮ್ರರ ಹಕ್ಕು ತಡೆಯುವವರು, ಸಜ್ಜನರಿಗೆ ಸಿದ್ಧಪಡಿಸಿದುದನ್ನು ಭಂಗಗೊಳಿಸುವವರು ನರಕಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾರೆ ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ವಿವರಿಸಿ ದಾತೃ-ಗ್ರಹೀತರ ಕರ್ತವ್ಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर श्राद्ध, देवकर्म और दान के ऋषि-विहित नियम पूछते हैं। भीष्म विस्तार से बताते हैं कि जो दीनों का हक रोकते हैं और जो सज्जन के लिए तैयार किए को बिगाड़ते हैं वे नरक जाते हैं, और दाता तथा ग्रहीता के कर्तव्य कहते हैं।","te":"శ్రాద్ధం, దైవకార్యం, దానానికి ఋషులు విధించిన నియమాలను యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. దీనుల హక్కును ఆపేవారు, సజ్జనుని కోసం సిద్ధం చేసినదాన్ని భంగపరిచేవారు నరకానికి పోతారని భీష్ముడు విపులంగా చెప్పి దాత, గ్రహీత కర్తవ్యాలు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"சிராத்தம், தெய்வ காரியம், தானத்துக்கு முனிவர்கள் விதித்த விதிகளை யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, எளியோரின் உரிமையைத் தடுப்போரும் நல்லவருக்கு ஒருக்கியதைக் கெடுப்போரும் நரகம் செல்வர் என்று பீஷ்மர் விரிவாகக் கூறி, கொடுப்பவன் பெறுபவனின் கடமைகளை உரைக்கிறார்.","ml":"ദേവന്മാർക്കും പിതൃക്കൾക്കും ഉള്ള ചടങ്ങുകളെയും ദാനത്തെയും കുറിച്ച് മുനിമാർ വെച്ച നിയമങ്ങൾ പറയണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. താഴ്ന്നവരുടെ അവകാശം തടഞ്ഞുവെക്കുന്നവരും, നല്ലവനുവേണ്ടി ഒരുക്കിയത് തകർക്കുന്നവരും നരകത്തിൽ പോകുമെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ വിസ്തരിച്ചു പറയുന്നു; ദാതാവിന്റെയും സ്വീകർത്താവിന്റെയും കടമകളും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.24; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"श्राद्धकाले च दैवे च धर्मे चापि पितामह ।\nइच्छामीह त्वयाख्यातं विहितं यत्सुरर्षिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, I wish you to tell me here what the divine sages have laid down for ancestral rites, for the gods' rites, and for dharma."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"दैवं पूर्वाह्णिके कुर्यादपराह्णे तु पैतृकम् ।\nमङ्गलाचारसंपन्नः कृतशौचः प्रयत्नवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should perform the rite of the gods in the forenoon and that of the ancestors in the afternoon, observing auspicious customs, purified and careful."}},{"n":3,"text":"मनुष्याणां तु मध्याह्ने प्रदद्यादुपपत्तितः ।\nकालहीनं तु यद्दानं तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should give to men at midday as appropriate. A gift made at the wrong time is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":4,"text":"लङ्घितं चावलीढं च कलिपूर्वं च यत्कृतम् ।\nरजस्वलाभिर्दृष्टं च तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What has been stepped over or licked, what was begun with a quarrel, and what has been seen by menstruating women is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":5,"text":"अवघुष्टं च यद्भुक्तमव्रतेन च भारत ।\nपरामृष्टं शुना चैव तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Food eaten after being announced aloud, or eaten by one without a vow, Bharata, or touched by a dog, is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":6,"text":"केशकीटावपतितं क्षुतं श्वभिरवेक्षितम् ।\nरुदितं चावधूतं च तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Food into which a hair or insect has fallen, or that was sneezed on, looked at by dogs, wept over or shaken is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":7,"text":"निरोंकारेण यद्भुक्तं सशस्त्रेण च भारत ।\nदुरात्मना च यद्भुक्तं तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Food eaten without Om, or with weapons in hand, Bharata, or eaten by a wicked person, is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":8,"text":"परोच्छिष्टं च यद्भुक्तं परिभुक्तं च यद्भवेत् ।\nदैवे पित्र्ये च सततं तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is eaten as another's leftovers or has been consumed in part, always in rites for gods or ancestors, is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":9,"text":"गर्हितं निन्दितं चैव परिविष्टं समन्युना ।\nदैवं वाप्यथ वा पैत्र्यं तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is censured or reviled, or served by someone angry, whether in a rite for the gods or the ancestors, is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":10,"text":"मन्त्रहीनं क्रियाहीनं यच्छ्राद्धं परिविष्यते ।\nत्रिभिर्वर्णैर्नरश्रेष्ठ तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A shraddha served without mantras and without rites, by men of the three classes, best of men, is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":11,"text":"आज्याहुतिं विना चैव यत्किंचित्परिविष्यते ।\nदुराचारैश्च यद्भुक्तं तं भागं रक्षसां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anything served without a ghee oblation, or eaten by those of evil conduct, is known as the share of the rakshasas."}},{"n":12,"text":"ये भागा रक्षसां प्रोक्तास्त उक्ता भरतर्षभ ।\nअत ऊर्ध्वं विसर्गस्य परीक्षां ब्राह्मणे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, I have told you which shares belong to the rakshasas. Next, hear the examination of a brahmin for the dismissal."}},{"n":13,"text":"यावन्तः पतिता विप्रा जडोन्मत्तास्तथैव च ।\nदैवे वाप्यथ वा पित्र्ये राजन्नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All fallen brahmins, dull or mad ones, king, are not fit to be invited, whether for the gods' or the ancestors' rites."}},{"n":14,"text":"श्वित्री कुष्ठी च क्लीबश्च तथा यक्ष्महतश्च यः ।\nअपस्मारी च यश्चान्धो राजन्नार्हन्ति सत्कृतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A leper, one with white skin disease, a eunuch, one afflicted with consumption, an epileptic or a blind man, king, deserves no honor."}},{"n":15,"text":"चिकित्सका देवलका वृथानियमधारिणः ।\nसोमविक्रयिणश्चैव श्राद्धे नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Physicians, temple priests, those who keep vows in vain, and sellers of soma are not fit to be invited to a shraddha."}},{"n":16,"text":"गायना नर्तकाश्चैव प्लवका वादकास्तथा ।\nकथका योधकाश्चैव राजन्नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Singers, dancers, acrobats, musicians, storytellers and fighters, king, are not fit to be invited."}},{"n":17,"text":"होतारो वृषलानां च वृषलाध्यापकास्तथा ।\nतथा वृषलशिष्याश्च राजन्नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Priests of shudras, teachers of shudras and disciples of shudras, king, are not fit to be invited."}},{"n":18,"text":"अनुयोक्ता च यो विप्रो अनुयुक्तश्च भारत ।\nनार्हतस्तावपि श्राद्धं ब्रह्मविक्रयिणौ हि तौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who asks questions and one who is questioned, Bharata, are not fit for shraddha, for they sell Brahman."}},{"n":19,"text":"अग्रणीर्यः कृतः पूर्वं वर्णावरपरिग्रहः ।\nब्राह्मणः सर्वविद्योऽपि राजन्नार्हति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who was first made a leader and takes in lower and other classes, king, is not fit, even if he knows every science."}},{"n":20,"text":"अनग्नयश्च ये विप्रा मृतनिर्यातकाश्च ये ।\nस्तेनाश्च पतिताश्चैव राजन्नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins without sacred fires, those who carry out the dead, thieves and the fallen, king, are not fit to be invited."}},{"n":21,"text":"अपरिज्ञातपूर्वाश्च गणपूर्वाश्च भारत ।\nपुत्रिकापूर्वपुत्राश्च श्राद्धे नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose background is unknown, those who belong to a band, and sons of appointed daughters, Bharata, are not fit for shraddha."}},{"n":22,"text":"ऋणकर्ता च यो राजन्यश्च वार्धुषिको द्विजः ।\nप्राणिविक्रयवृत्तिश्च राजन्नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who incurs debts, king, a brahmin moneylender, and one who lives by selling living beings are not fit to be invited."}},{"n":23,"text":"स्त्रीपूर्वाः काण्डपृष्ठाश्च यावन्तो भरतर्षभ ।\nअजपा ब्राह्मणाश्चैव श्राद्धे नार्हन्ति केतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are ruled by women, those who have arrows on their backs, best of Bharatas, and brahmins who do not chant are not fit for shraddha."}},{"n":24,"text":"श्राद्धे दैवे च निर्दिष्टा ब्राह्मणा भरतर्षभ ।\nदातुः प्रतिग्रहीतुश्च शृणुष्वानुग्रहं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of Bharatas, I have told you which brahmins are barred in shraddha and gods' rites. Now hear again the favor to giver and receiver."}},{"n":25,"text":"चीर्णव्रता गुणैर्युक्ता भवेयुर्येऽपि कर्षकाः ।\nसावित्रीज्ञाः क्रियावन्तस्ते राजन्केतनक्षमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even cultivators, king, who have kept their vows and have good qualities, know the Savitri and perform rites, are fit to be invited."}},{"n":26,"text":"क्षात्रधर्मिणमप्याजौ केतयेत्कुलजं द्विजम् ।\nन त्वेव वणिजं तात श्राद्धेषु परिकल्पयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One may invite even a well-born brahmin of warrior's dharma in a battle, but never, dear one, should one appoint a merchant at shraddhas."}},{"n":27,"text":"अग्निहोत्री च यो विप्रो ग्रामवासी च यो भवेत् ।\nअस्तेनश्चातिथिज्ञश्च स राजन्केतनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who keeps the sacred fire, lives in a village, is not a thief, and knows how to treat guests is fit to be invited, king."}},{"n":28,"text":"सावित्रीं जपते यस्तु त्रिकालं भरतर्षभ ।\nभिक्षावृत्तिः क्रियावांश्च स राजन्केतनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who recites the Savitri at three times of day, best of Bharatas, lives by alms and performs rites is fit to be invited, king."}},{"n":29,"text":"उदितास्तमितो यश्च तथैवास्तमितोदितः ।\nअहिंस्रश्चाल्पदोषश्च स राजन्केतनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is up from sunrise to sunset and the reverse, who is not violent and has few faults, is fit to be invited, king."}},{"n":30,"text":"अकल्कको ह्यतर्कश्च ब्राह्मणो भरतर्षभ ।\nससंज्ञो भैक्ष्यवृत्तिश्च स राजन्केतनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who is without deceit and without argument, who is self-aware and lives by alms, is fit to be invited, king."}},{"n":31,"text":"अव्रती कितवः स्तेनः प्राणिविक्रय्यथो वणिक् ।\nपश्चाच्च पीतवान्सोमं स राजन्केतनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who was without vows, a gambler, a thief, a seller of living beings, or a merchant, but later drank soma, is fit to be invited, king."}},{"n":32,"text":"अर्जयित्वा धनं पूर्वं दारुणैः कृषिकर्मभिः ।\nभवेत्सर्वातिथिः पश्चात्स राजन्केतनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who earned wealth first through harsh farming and later became a host to all guests is fit to be invited, king."}},{"n":33,"text":"ब्रह्मविक्रयनिर्दिष्टं स्त्रिया यच्चार्जितं धनम् ।\nअदेयं पितृदेवेभ्यो यच्च क्लैब्यादुपार्जितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealth that is declared to come from selling Brahman, that earned by a woman, and that gained through unmanliness is not to be given to the ancestors or gods."}},{"n":34,"text":"क्रियमाणेऽपवर्गे तु यो द्विजो भरतर्षभ ।\nन व्याहरति यद्युक्तं तस्याधर्मो गवानृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of Bharatas, a brahmin who does not say what is proper when the dismissal is performed incurs the sin of a false statement about a cow."}},{"n":35,"text":"श्राद्धस्य ब्राह्मणः कालः प्राप्तं दधि घृतं तथा ।\nसोमक्षयश्च मांसं च यदारण्यं युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin's time for shraddha has come, with curd, ghee, the waning moon and forest meat, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":36,"text":"श्राद्धापवर्गे विप्रस्य स्वधा वै स्वदिता भवेत् ।\nक्षत्रियस्याप्यथो ब्रूयात्प्रीयन्तां पितरस्त्विति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the close of a shraddha a brahmin says 'Svadha', and one should say to a kshatriya, 'May the ancestors be pleased.'"}},{"n":37,"text":"अपवर्गे तु वैश्यस्य श्राद्धकर्मणि भारत ।\nअक्षय्यमभिधातव्यं स्वस्ति शूद्रस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the close of a shraddha rite for a vaishya, Bharata, one should say 'Akshayya'; for a shudra, 'Svasti.'"}},{"n":38,"text":"पुण्याहवाचनं दैवे ब्राह्मणस्य विधीयते ।\nएतदेव निरोंकारं क्षत्रियस्य विधीयते ।\nवैश्यस्य चैव वक्तव्यं प्रीयन्तां देवता इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The 'Punyaha' blessing is prescribed for a brahmin in the gods' rite; the same without Om is prescribed for a kshatriya, and for a vaishya one should say, 'May the gods be pleased.'"}},{"n":39,"text":"कर्मणामानुपूर्वीं च विधिपूर्वकृतं शृणु ।\nजातकर्मादिकान्सर्वांस्त्रिषु वर्णेषु भारत ।\nब्रह्मक्षत्रे हि मन्त्रोक्ता वैश्यस्य च युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear the order of rites as ordained in the earlier rule: jatakarma and all the rest for the three classes, Bharata, are by mantra for brahmins and kshatriyas, and, Yudhishthira, for the vaishya too."}},{"n":40,"text":"विप्रस्य रशना मौञ्जी मौर्वी राजन्यगामिनी ।\nबाल्वजीत्येव वैश्यस्य धर्म एष युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a brahmin the girdle is of munja grass, for a kshatriya of moorva, and for a vaishya of balbaja; this is the rule, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":41,"text":"दातुः प्रतिग्रहीतुश्च धर्माधर्माविमौ शृणु ।\nब्राह्मणस्यानृतेऽधर्मः प्रोक्तः पातकसंज्ञितः ।\nचतुर्गुणः क्षत्रियस्य वैश्यस्याष्टगुणः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now hear the dharma and adharma of the giver and the receiver. For a brahmin, falsehood is declared a sin called a grave offense; for a kshatriya it is fourfold and for a vaishya eightfold."}},{"n":42,"text":"नान्यत्र ब्राह्मणोऽश्नीयात्पूर्वं विप्रेण केतितः ।\nयवीयान्पशुहिंसायां तुल्यधर्मो भवेत्स हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who has been invited first by a brahmin should not eat elsewhere. If a junior does, he bears equal guilt in the slaying of animals."}},{"n":43,"text":"अथ राजन्यवैश्याभ्यां यद्यश्नीयात्तु केतितः ।\nयवीयान्पशुहिंसायां भागार्धं समवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if one invited eats at the house of a kshatriya or vaishya, the junior takes half of the share of guilt in killing animals."}},{"n":44,"text":"दैवं वाप्यथ वा पित्र्यं योऽश्नीयाद्ब्राह्मणादिषु ।\nअस्नातो ब्राह्मणो राजंस्तस्याधर्मो गवानृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, a brahmin who has not bathed and eats a rite for gods or ancestors with brahmins incurs the sin of a false statement about a cow."}},{"n":45,"text":"आशौचो ब्राह्मणो राजन्योऽश्नीयाद्ब्राह्मणादिषु ।\nज्ञानपूर्वमथो लोभात्तस्याधर्मो गवानृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who is impure and eats with brahmins, knowingly and out of greed, incurs the sin of a false statement about a cow."}},{"n":46,"text":"अन्नेनान्नं च यो लिप्सेत्कर्मार्थं चैव भारत ।\nआमन्त्रयति राजेन्द्र तस्याधर्मोऽनृतं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, one who hopes to gain food through food, or invites for the sake of a rite, bears the sin of falsehood."}},{"n":47,"text":"अवेदव्रतचारित्रास्त्रिभिर्वर्णैर्युधिष्ठिर ।\nमन्त्रवत्परिविष्यन्ते तेष्वधर्मो गवानृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, if brahmins ignorant of the Vedas, vows and conduct are served with mantras by those of three classes, the sin of a false statement about a cow falls on them."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":48,"text":"पित्र्यं वाप्यथ वा दैवं दीयते यत्पितामह ।\nएतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं दत्तं येषु महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, I wish to hear to whom a gift, whether for ancestors or gods, bears great fruit."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":49,"text":"येषां दाराः प्रतीक्षन्ते सुवृष्टिमिव कर्षकाः ।\nउच्छेषपरिशेषं हि तान्भोजय युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Feed those whose wives wait for them as farmers wait for good rain, with what is left over, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":50,"text":"चारित्रनियता राजन्ये कृशाः कृशवृत्तयः ।\nअर्थिनश्चोपगच्छन्ति तेषु दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to those, king, who are bound by conduct, are thin and live thinly, and come to ask for things."}},{"n":51,"text":"तद्भक्तास्तद्गृहा राजंस्तद्धनास्तदपाश्रयाः ।\nअर्थिनश्च भवन्त्यर्थे तेषु दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to those who are devoted to him, whose houses and wealth are his and who depend on him, and who in need come for something."}},{"n":52,"text":"तस्करेभ्यः परेभ्यो वा ये भयार्ता युधिष्ठिर ।\nअर्थिनो भोक्तुमिच्छन्ति तेषु दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to those, Yudhishthira, who are afraid of thieves or enemies and wish to eat."}},{"n":53,"text":"अकल्ककस्य विप्रस्य भैक्षोत्करकृतात्मनः ।\nबटवो यस्य भिक्षन्ति तेभ्यो दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to those for whom the students of a deceitless brahmin, who lives by gathered alms, beg."}},{"n":54,"text":"हृतस्वा हृतदाराश्च ये विप्रा देशसंप्लवे ।\nअर्थार्थमभिगच्छन्ति तेभ्यो दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to brahmins who have lost wealth and wives in a country's ruin and come seeking wealth."}},{"n":55,"text":"व्रतिनो नियमस्थाश्च ये विप्राः श्रुतसंमताः ।\nतत्समाप्त्यर्थमिच्छन्ति तेषु दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to brahmins keeping vows and observances, respected for learning, who seek to complete them."}},{"n":56,"text":"अव्युत्क्रान्ताश्च धर्मेषु पाषण्डसमयेषु च ।\nकृशप्राणाः कृशधनास्तेषु दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to those who have not transgressed dharma or sects, and are of thin vitality and wealth."}},{"n":57,"text":"कृतसर्वस्वहरणा निर्दोषाः प्रभविष्णुभिः ।\nस्पृहयन्ति च भुक्तान्नं तेषु दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to the blameless whose all has been taken away by the powerful, who long for a cooked meal."}},{"n":58,"text":"तपस्विनस्तपोनिष्ठास्तेषां भैक्षचराश्च ये ।\nअर्थिनः किंचिदिच्छन्ति तेषु दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts bear great fruit to ascetics devoted to austerity and to their alms-wanderers who ask for something."}},{"n":59,"text":"महाफलविधिर्दाने श्रुतस्ते भरतर्षभ ।\nनिरयं येन गच्छन्ति स्वर्गं चैव हि तच्छृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of Bharatas, you have heard the rule of greatly fruitful giving. Now hear the ways people go to hell and to heaven."}},{"n":60,"text":"गुर्वर्थं वाभयार्थं वा वर्जयित्वा युधिष्ठिर ।\nयेऽनृतं कथयन्ति स्म ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, except for a teacher's sake or to relieve fear, those who speak falsely go to hell."}},{"n":61,"text":"परदाराभिहर्तारः परदाराभिमर्शिनः ।\nपरदारप्रयोक्तारस्ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who abduct others' wives, touch others' wives or employ others' wives go to hell."}},{"n":62,"text":"ये परस्वापहर्तारः परस्वानां च नाशकाः ।\nसूचकाश्च परेषां ये ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who steal others' property, destroy others' property or are informers against others go to hell."}},{"n":63,"text":"प्रपाणां च सभानां च संक्रमाणां च भारत ।\nअगाराणां च भेत्तारो नरा निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, those who destroy water-huts, assembly halls, bridges and houses go to hell."}},{"n":64,"text":"अनाथां प्रमदां बालां वृद्धां भीतां तपस्विनीम् ।\nवञ्चयन्ति नरा ये च ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who cheat helpless women, girls, the old, the frightened or female ascetics go to hell."}},{"n":65,"text":"वृत्तिच्छेदं गृहच्छेदं दारच्छेदं च भारत ।\nमित्रच्छेदं तथाशायास्ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who cut off a person's livelihood, home, wife or friend, or someone's hope, go to hell."}},{"n":66,"text":"सूचकाः संधिभेत्तारः परवृत्त्युपजीवकाः ।\nअकृतज्ञाश्च मित्राणां ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Informers, those who break agreements, those who live on others' livelihood and ingrates to friends go to hell."}},{"n":67,"text":"पाषण्डा दूषकाश्चैव समयानां च दूषकाः ।\nये प्रत्यवसिताश्चैव ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heretics, slanderers, those who spoil agreements, and those who have returned to deceit go to hell."}},{"n":68,"text":"कृताशं कृतनिर्वेशं कृतभक्तं कृतश्रमम् ।\nभेदैर्ये व्यपकर्षन्ति ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who by tricks draw away a person who was hoping, has been fixed up, has been fed and has worked go to hell."}},{"n":69,"text":"पर्यश्नन्ति च ये दारानग्निभृत्यातिथींस्तथा ।\nउत्सन्नपितृदेवेज्यास्ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who eat before wives, fire, servants and guests, who neglect rites to ancestors and gods, go to hell."}},{"n":70,"text":"वेदविक्रयिणश्चैव वेदानां चैव दूषकाः ।\nवेदानां लेखकाश्चैव ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sellers of the Vedas, slanderers of the Vedas, and writers of the Vedas go to hell."}},{"n":71,"text":"चातुराश्रम्यबाह्याश्च श्रुतिबाह्याश्च ये नराः ।\nविकर्मभिश्च जीवन्ति ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men outside the four stages and outside the Shruti, who live by wrong actions, go to hell."}},{"n":72,"text":"केशविक्रयिका राजन्विषविक्रयिकाश्च ये ।\nक्षीरविक्रयिकाश्चैव ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sellers of hair, king, sellers of poison and sellers of milk go to hell."}},{"n":73,"text":"ब्राह्मणानां गवां चैव कन्यानां च युधिष्ठिर ।\nयेऽन्तरं यान्ति कार्येषु ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, those who intervene against brahmins, cows and maidens in their affairs go to hell."}},{"n":74,"text":"शस्त्रविक्रयकाश्चैव कर्तारश्च युधिष्ठिर ।\nशल्यानां धनुषां चैव ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sellers of weapons and makers of arrows and bows, Yudhishthira, go to hell."}},{"n":75,"text":"शल्यैर्वा शङ्कुभिर्वापि श्वभ्रैर्वा भरतर्षभ ।\nये मार्गमनुरुन्धन्ति ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of Bharatas, those who block a road with arrows, stakes or pits go to hell."}},{"n":76,"text":"उपाध्यायांश्च भृत्यांश्च भक्तांश्च भरतर्षभ ।\nये त्यजन्त्यसमर्थांस्तांस्ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who abandon teachers, servants and devotees who are helpless, best of Bharatas, go to hell."}},{"n":77,"text":"अप्राप्तदमकाश्चैव नासानां वेधकास्तथा ।\nबन्धकाश्च पशूनां ये ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who punish before the time, pierce noses or confine cattle go to hell."}},{"n":78,"text":"अगोप्तारश्छलद्रव्या बलिषड्भागतत्पराः ।\nसमर्थाश्चाप्यदातारस्ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who do not protect, who take things by deceit, who are intent on a sixth share as tax, and who are able but do not give go to hell."}},{"n":79,"text":"क्षान्तान्दान्तांस्तथा प्राज्ञान्दीर्घकालं सहोषितान् ।\nत्यजन्ति कृतकृत्या ये ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who, having had their purpose met, abandon the patient, self-controlled and wise who lived with them long go to hell."}},{"n":80,"text":"बालानामथ वृद्धानां दासानां चैव ये नराः ।\nअदत्त्वा भक्षयन्त्यग्रे ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who eat first without giving to children, the old and the servants go to hell."}},{"n":81,"text":"एते पूर्वर्षिभिर्दृष्टाः प्रोक्ता निरयगामिनः ।\nभागिनः स्वर्गलोकस्य वक्ष्यामि भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are the ones the earlier sages saw and named as going to hell. Best of Bharatas, I will now tell you who share in heaven."}},{"n":82,"text":"सर्वेष्वेव तु कार्येषु दैवपूर्वेषु भारत ।\nहन्ति पुत्रान्पशून्कृत्स्नान्ब्राह्मणातिक्रमः कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, in all rites that begin with the gods, an offense against brahmins destroys one's sons and all one's cattle."}},{"n":83,"text":"दानेन तपसा चैव सत्येन च युधिष्ठिर ।\nये धर्ममनुवर्तन्ते ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, men who follow dharma through giving, austerity and truth go to heaven."}},{"n":84,"text":"शुश्रूषाभिस्तपोभिश्च श्रुतमादाय भारत ।\nये प्रतिग्रहनिःस्नेहास्ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, men who, having gained learning through service and austerities, are free from desire for gifts go to heaven."}},{"n":85,"text":"भयात्पापात्तथाबाधाद्दारिद्र्याद्व्याधिधर्षणात् ।\nयत्कृते प्रतिमुच्यन्ते ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men who free others from fear, sin, distress, poverty and the attack of disease go to heaven."}},{"n":86,"text":"क्षमावन्तश्च धीराश्च धर्मकार्येषु चोत्थिताः ।\nमङ्गलाचारयुक्ताश्च ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are patient and steady, are active in works of dharma and have auspicious conduct go to heaven."}},{"n":87,"text":"निवृत्ता मधुमांसेभ्यः परदारेभ्य एव च ।\nनिवृत्ताश्चैव मद्येभ्यस्ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who abstain from honey, meat, others' wives and liquor go to heaven."}},{"n":88,"text":"आश्रमाणां च कर्तारः कुलानां चैव भारत ।\nदेशानां नगराणां च ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, those who found hermitages, families, regions and cities go to heaven."}},{"n":89,"text":"वस्त्राभरणदातारो भक्षपानान्नदास्तथा ।\nकुटुम्बानां च दातारस्ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who give clothes, ornaments, food and drink and provide for households go to heaven."}},{"n":90,"text":"सर्वहिंसानिवृत्ताश्च नराः सर्वसहाश्च ये ।\nसर्वस्याश्रयभूताश्च ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men who abstain from all violence, endure all things, and are a refuge for all go to heaven."}},{"n":91,"text":"मातरं पितरं चैव शुश्रूषन्ति जितेन्द्रियाः ।\nभ्रातॄणां चैव सस्नेहास्ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who, with senses mastered, serve mother and father and are affectionate toward their brothers go to heaven."}},{"n":92,"text":"आढ्याश्च बलवन्तश्च यौवनस्थाश्च भारत ।\nये वै जितेन्द्रिया धीरास्ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, those who are rich, strong and in youth, and yet have mastered their senses and are steady, go to heaven."}},{"n":93,"text":"अपराद्धेषु सस्नेहा मृदवो मित्रवत्सलाः ।\nआराधनसुखाश्चापि ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are kind toward the offending, gentle, friendly and easily pleased go to heaven."}},{"n":94,"text":"सहस्रपरिवेष्टारस्तथैव च सहस्रदाः ।\nत्रातारश्च सहस्राणां पुरुषाः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men who maintain a thousand, give a thousand, and rescue thousands go to heaven."}},{"n":95,"text":"सुवर्णस्य च दातारो गवां च भरतर्षभ ।\nयानानां वाहनानां च ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of Bharatas, givers of gold, cows, carriages and mounts go to heaven."}},{"n":96,"text":"वैवाहिकानां कन्यानां प्रेष्याणां च युधिष्ठिर ।\nदातारो वाससां चैव ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, those who give brides for marriage, servants and clothes go to heaven."}},{"n":97,"text":"विहारावसथोद्यानकूपारामसभाप्रदाः ।\nवप्राणां चैव कर्तारस्ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who give pleasure houses, lodgings, gardens, wells, groves, halls and who make embankments go to heaven."}},{"n":98,"text":"निवेशनानां क्षेत्राणां वसतीनां च भारत ।\nदातारः प्रार्थितानां च ते नराः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, those who give houses, fields and dwellings, and give to those who ask, go to heaven."}},{"n":99,"text":"रसानामथ बीजानां धान्यानां च युधिष्ठिर ।\nस्वयमुत्पाद्य दातारः पुरुषाः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, men who produce juices, seeds and grains themselves and give them go to heaven."}},{"n":100,"text":"यस्मिन्कस्मिन्कुले जाता बहुपुत्राः शतायुषः ।\nसानुक्रोशा जितक्रोधाः पुरुषाः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men born into any family who have many sons, live a hundred years, and are merciful and have conquered anger go to heaven."}},{"n":101,"text":"एतदुक्तममुत्रार्थं दैवं पित्र्यं च भारत ।\nधर्माधर्मौ च दानस्य यथा पूर्वर्षिभिः कृतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, this has been told for the sake of the next world: the rites for gods and ancestors, and the dharma and adharma of giving as the earlier sages made them."}}]}]}